WEBVTT

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.850
Eiko...

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.140
LONG CATS OF THE WORLD

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.200
Eiko?

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.580
NAGOMI

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.580
SUGOMI

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.420
Good morning.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.560
Time to switch to summer uniforms!

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:25.770
Yeah!

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.770
KAMURI'S FLUFFY

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.440
Ice cream in the morning...

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.360
Because we're wearing summer uniforms!

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.320
Do you want some ice cream, too, Hana?

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.280
Here, have a lick!

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.240
Two licks! No, three licks!

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.070
Don't be shy!

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.290
What does ice cream have to do
with summer uniforms?

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.040
Even you, Eiko!

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.170
Well, when you switch
from winter to summer uniforms,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.460
you feel so much lighter
that it makes you nervous, right?

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.130
Oh, I know!

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.170
Feeling like something's missing!

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.550
That's right!

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.350
Morning, Kamu.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.810
Morning, Kamu!

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.220
Good morning!

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.440
Is something wrong?

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:11.770
Are you hungry?

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.400
I'm not hungry. Lick.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:16.940
Listen...

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.410
I forgot to put on the skirt.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.570
What?

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:24.780
Whaaat?

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.120
Wh-Wh-What should we do?

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.120
What should we do?
Wh-Wh-What should we do?

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.370
Oh, boy.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.630
We switched to summer uniforms,
but that's taking off too much.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.630
I thought the cool feeling on my legs
was from not wearing tights.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.260
I see!

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.350
Then I'll be able to see your bare legs
every day from now on, huh, Kamu?

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:45.810
A sight for sore eyes!

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:46.850
Guys!

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.350
How can you be so calm about it?

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.690
Because you're stressed out enough
for all of us, Hana!

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:53.980
Maybe?

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:56.150
A-A-After all...

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.780
Under that shirt are her...

00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.650
p-p-pan...

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:00.740
...ties!

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:01.700
Yes!

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.950
Huh? But if you say that...

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.370
We're just wearing panties, too...

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:07.950
under here.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.120
Then it's okay not to wear a skirt?

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.710
Or it's okay not to wear panties?

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.840
Hana, panties are not included
in the snack category!

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.300
Well, think of it this way...

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:24.140
It's not like she forgot
to wear panties.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.350
I remembered.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.680
U-Um...

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.890
But still, it's not good, is it?
Isn't it a problem?

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.440
For the rest of the day?
And going home?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.980
Here, Kamu. My gym uniform.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:39.940
Strap.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:45.320
H-Huh? Is that all there is to it?

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.370
This solves it?

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.700
That solves everything!

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:50.870
Huh?

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.710
Really?

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.040
You were overthinking it, Hana.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.340
You should take things easier.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:04.970
Eiko...

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.640
Yeah.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.850
Still,

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:12.730
how did you forget to put on a skirt?

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.390
Actually...

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.110
What is it?

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:26.200
You were preoccupied with thoughts
of a lightly-dressed Eiko!

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:27.620
I can see that!

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:28.580
I don't think so.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:34.710
Well, Eiko, students were selling
photos of you in middle school!

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:35.960
What?

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.460
Here's a pic from back then!

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.710
Why did you buy that?

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.590
The graduation memorial price.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.180
It was on sale for 80% off,
and I couldn't help it!

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:49.050
My photos were selling at cheap prices,
and I didn't even know.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:51.220
But it was just an impulse buy.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.890
I don't really need it.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.020
So you can have it, Kamu!

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.650
Th-Thank you, Tama.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.570
She smiled! She smiled at me!

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.070
My heart skipped a beat!

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:11.080
Kamu, what are you gonna do with that?

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.580
My parents will be happy
if I show it to them.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.080
They'll probably frame it
and hang it on a wall.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.340
What does your family think of me?

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:25.550
What's wrong?

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:28.300
Eiko, is this you?

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.140
Yeah, that's me.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.850
That's definitely Eiko.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:41.110
So you didn't wear hairpins
in middle school, Eiko.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.860
Oh, you probably didn't recognize her
without the hairpins.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:47.110
Is that such an important part
of my appearance?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.610
Hairpins...

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:51.320
Hairpins are a part of your body, Eiko.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.870
Part of my body?

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:56.080
Then ribbons are part of your body,
right, Tama?

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:06.260
Oh, welcome home, Ms. Hannen.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:08.430
Yes.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:09.760
I'm back.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:12.300
Were you out shopping again today?

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.680
Yes! I got tired of going to the same
convenience store all the time!

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.560
So I mastered all of the convenience
stores in this area!

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.980
I'm able to go to any convenience store
within five kilometers of here!

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:27.440
Congratulations!

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:28.900
But it seems like

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.200
you're getting further away
from the meaning of "convenience."

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.200
Definition: Something conducive. Favorable. Useful.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.200
CONDUCIVE. FAVORABLE.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:36.660
Oh...

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:43.710
I'm glad they refilled the flavors
that were sold out before.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:44.750
Yep.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.270
U-Um, Kamuri...

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:01.190
What are you so lost in thought about?

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.270
That photo...

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.780
It's different from the Eiko I saw last year.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:18.120
I walked by her in the shopping district.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:21.290
A girl with long hair
and who looked exactly like Eiko...

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:25.290
But the Eiko in the photo has short hair.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.540
It's not her.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.420
Now that you mention it,

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:31.130
I also walked by a girl

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:34.180
who looked a lot like Eiko
in the bookstore downtown.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.680
I realized it wasn't her,

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:39.310
but maybe she has a double?

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.060
I don't know. But...

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:45.190
I was able to meet her then...

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:46.310
Huh?

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:47.400
No...

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:48.860
Nothing.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:52.200
Teacher!

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:54.200
What?

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:55.700
Huh?

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.910
Why are you wearing sweatpants?

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.950
Since this is the uniform-switching day,

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.410
I thought I'd play along,

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.420
but I was told off by the head teacher.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.000
Oh, so that's what happened.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.250
I see.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:13.880
Now you've got me totally curious
about your blunder.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:17.640
I bet it's not even close
to what you have in mind.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.100
What I have in mind...

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.430
Don't tell me you wet your...

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:25.690
Not another word.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.570
Well, you two better be careful also.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:31.860
The rules inspection is coming up.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:33.360
Right.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:38.070
I heard some schools check your panties
during the rules inspection!

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.080
Be glad you don't go there.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.750
I'm sure Eiko would be in trouble for that.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:45.750
What?

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.380
What, are your panties that flashy?

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.130
No, not especially—

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:50.960
Let's see.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:55.680
I think you'd be fine with those.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:56.930
Oh...

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.140
Really?

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:00.470
Of course, right?

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.180
Ms. Enami!

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:05.140
Yeah, what is it?

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.200
Wh-What's the matter,

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:19.570
Eiko?

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:21.530
Before you two got here,

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:23.450
a super-lethal move was played,

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:26.250
making Eiko's mental gauge take a nosedive!

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:34.510
Pet-pet-pet-pet-pet.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.970
Her mental gauge is making a comeback!

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.390
What's a gauge?

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:42.390
There. There.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:43.850
There. There.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.350
There. There.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.690
There. There. There.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:50.980
Huh? What?

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:01.530
Wanna stop at a convenience store
on the way home?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:03.790
I hear they've got a new kind of ice cream!

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.200
What? Didn't you have
ice cream this morning?

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.160
No, no.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:11.130
School ice cream and outside ice cream
are two totally different things.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.380
SUNDIAL AND CLOCK

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.380
It's like the difference
between a sundial and a clock!

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.960
SUN CLOCK

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.960
S-Sundial and clock?

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.170
Hana...

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:18.550
Kamuri...

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:21.550
I forgot to return the gym uniform.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:26.310
That's because Eiko was in a hurry today,
so she left before us.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:28.140
Did she have something to do?

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:29.560
I have to return them.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.190
But if you return them here,

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:33.820
you'll just be wearing panties, Kamu—

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:35.820
I got here fine, so it's no problem.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.360
No!

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:46.370
Eiko said something about going
to the shopping district.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:48.200
Should we track her down?

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.710
Kamuri, the shopping district...

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.300
I see, I see!

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:58.720
Eiko's double, huh?

00:11:59.130 --> 00:11:59.880
Yeah.

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:03.090
Kamu and I both saw her.

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:07.970
Maybe that's her doppelganger!

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:11.480
"Doped-up gangbanger"?

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:13.610
"Doppelganger"!

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:14.730
You know...

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:17.230
like the fairies in Tohoku!

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:19.690
Fairies?

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:25.580
They look just like you.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:27.240
Yeah!

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.330
In other words, like a body double!

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.130
Like military leaders used to use!

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:38.050
Another me is going to appear?

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:39.670
That's bad news.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:42.470
This town isn't big enough
for two supreme rulers!

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.010
Like that?

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:45.760
Supreme ruler?

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:56.730
If the real Eiko meets her doppelganger...

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:58.820
I-If they meet?

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:01.570
...one of them will die.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:02.820
Die?

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:05.780
What?

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:08.910
There's no escape!

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:11.660
I finally found you, my fake self.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.880
That's the law of the village!

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:18.210
The village?

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:21.010
You can't defy the law of the village.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.010
E-Eiko's going to be killed

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.930
by a fairy, a military body double,
a supreme ruler and the law of the village?

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:29.180
Hana, you can treat that
with some skepticism.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:30.850
It's a lie?

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:32.180
It's a little bit true.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:36.400
Well, it's like an urban legend.

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:38.480
That aside, I have to return these.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:42.490
Eiko!

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:46.610
Oh no! That's where I saw
her doppler-ganger!

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:48.740
Doppelganger.

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:49.450
Eiko!

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.120
I'll save you!

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:02.880
<i>There she is!</i>

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:05.340
Kamuri?

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:16.560
Eiko?

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:22.110
Yes. I'm Eiko.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.190
- Whaaat?
- Whaaat?

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.450
What are you guys doing here?

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:31.830
Eiko and h-her pom-peri-danger!

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.080
Wh-Wh-What should we do?

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:39.420
Th-This time for sure, we need to use
our magical girl combo power!

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:46.300
Get away...

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:47.630
...from her!

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:48.680
Get away...

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:50.260
...from her!

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:51.260
Get away...

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:52.930
...from her!

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.520
- Get away from her!
- Get away from her!

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.020
- Get away from her!
- Get away from her!

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.610
I don't know what you're doing,
but I'll introduce you.

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:02.940
This is my little sister, Miki.

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:04.280
- Get a—
- Get a—

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.950
Come on, there are no doppelgangers!

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:14.240
I've been looking
for a reference book recently.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:17.250
Today I asked my sister for advice.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.750
So that's why I saw you
at the bookstore before...

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:23.800
The look-alike was Sis-sauce!

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:26.840
I totally forgot you had a sister.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:27.510
Yep.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:31.300
That was a while back,
the last time I mentioned Mickey.

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:32.640
It's Miki.

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:34.970
I see. Mickey, huh?

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:36.100
Miki.

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:39.270
Why did you say you were Eiko before?

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.770
Well, that's because...

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:51.200
I thought maybe that was the right answer
for the situation.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.620
No, I think that was the wrong answer.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.950
I see. You learn something new everyday.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.830
Kamu, do we look so similar
that you can't tell us apart?

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:07.550
No. She looks like you
when you were in elementary school, Eiko.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.260
Maybe the hairstyle?

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.220
Come to think of it, Sister,

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:16.060
you had long hair
back in elementary school.

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:19.520
Also,

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:23.730
I spotted Eiko on the street
this time last year.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:29.190
<i>E-Eiko...</i>

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.070
<i>Hello?</i>

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:34.410
<i>Eiko...</i>

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:35.450
<i>That's right.</i>

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.830
<i>U-Um...</i>

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:43.920
<i>Yes. Hoshio Girls' High School.</i>

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:45.920
<i>Yes, that school.</i>

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:54.640
<i>Hoshio...</i>

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:56.850
<i>Girls'...</i>

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:03.730
I thought it was
the middle school Eiko at the time.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.770
So it was Mickey...

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:06.730
It's Miki.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.780
But you looked different in that photo, so...

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:14.700
I see.

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:17.450
That's why you had the strange reaction
when you saw the photo, huh?

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:19.950
Yep.

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:23.960
But then, when you first saw me
after high school started,

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.710
didn't you have a feeling
that something was off?

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:29.210
I thought you were just
making your high school debut.

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:35.720
But you hadn't changed a bit
since elementary school, Kamu.

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:39.010
That's what surprised me.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.390
You told me that before.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:43.600
You were that surprised?

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:44.770
Yeah.

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:48.610
I'd missed you so much

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.610
that I thought
maybe you were just a hallucination.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:57.780
Ow, that hurts!

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:04.790
Tell me, Kamu...

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:08.500
Did you take Hoshio's
high school entrance exam

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.750
because you thought
I might be going there?

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:15.260
Jeez.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:19.260
Just because that's the school I'm interested in
doesn't mean I'd go there.

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:22.640
What were you intending to do
if it turned out I wasn't going there?

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:24.480
A shy girl like you...

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:27.350
I-I would've gotten by somehow.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:30.110
I wonder.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:31.360
I have gotten...

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:32.610
by...

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.160
Eiko...

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:40.280
Um...

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:45.460
I was thinking about you this morning

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:47.540
and that's why I forgot my skirt.

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.500
You were thinking about me?

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:51.670
All that time...

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:53.840
All that time...

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:56.090
I missed you!

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:01.640
I'm so happy...

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:03.850
that I got to see you again!

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:05.560
Me, too.

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:07.730
That I really got to see you.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:09.020
Me, too.

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:13.190
Kamu, thank you.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.950
"Thank you" is my line.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:20.240
Huh? You mean my line.

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:22.030
No, mine.

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:24.240
No, it's mine.

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:26.200
- No, mine.
- No, mine.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.290
No, mine!

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.670
- No, mine!
- No, mine!

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:33.170
It's so moving!

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:35.090
Yes, I've learned something.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:36.510
Learned what?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.130
Sneeze!

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:43.850
You're together now because your
little sister said our school's name!

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.810
It's like the gears of fate are entangled.

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:49.560
I'm not sure the gears would work
if they were entangled.

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:53.150
But Kamu, the school you were in before
would've gotten you

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.780
into their affiliated high school
without a test, right?

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:56.940
Yep.

00:19:57.190 --> 00:20:00.780
I'm surprised your parents let you take
the entrance exam for an outside school.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:03.870
When I told them Eiko might be going there,

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.370
they agreed right away.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:08.790
They wished me good luck.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:12.790
So again, how does your family
handle me, Kamu?

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:16.500
I'm going to take
the entrance exam next year.

00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:17.760
I'll do my best.

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:19.720
<i>Entrance exam?</i>

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:23.050
<i>If someone who's going to take
the entrance exam is around me,</i>

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:24.550
<i>it might be bad luck for them!</i>

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:29.520
<i>What if breathing the same air causes her
to be cursed by the gap year?</i>

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:32.650
Hana...

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:35.320
Why are you holding your breath?

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:37.820
The air...

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:39.240
I see.

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:40.950
When you become a high school student,

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:46.080
the expression "not breathing a word"
becomes more than just an idiom.

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:48.240
You embody it.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:49.790
I'm learning.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:53.420
H-Hana!

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.040
I see. I'm learning.

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:57.500
I-I don't think you are.

00:22:40.020 --> 00:22:41.400
Kamuri, good morning!

00:22:41.650 --> 00:22:42.730
Good morning.

00:22:46.700 --> 00:22:47.700
Cat!

00:22:48.410 --> 00:22:49.950
How cute!

00:22:50.490 --> 00:22:51.790
Come here!

00:22:55.210 --> 00:22:57.670
Eiko is like a cat whisperer.

00:22:57.920 --> 00:22:59.040
Oh, really?

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:01.130
Eiko is amazing!

00:23:01.130 --> 00:23:01.800
Yep.

00:23:06.880 --> 00:23:08.220
Not only cats.

00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:11.930
I'd say Eiko is a "Kamuri whisperer," too!

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:19.060
U-Um, s-sorry...

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:20.440
I didn't mean...

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:32.080
What?

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.080
I forgot my skirt again.

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:37.160
Whaaat?
